    "detailed_description": "Sometime in the near past, a kid gets an ominous television transmission.<br />\r\nHe has intercepted a cryptic message - and the Deathchron arrives at his house.<br />\r\nHe is transported to an alternate future world, where robotic mechs have taken over,<br />\r\nand he has one chance to save the world. A.R.T. - his own automated robot transporter is<br />\r\nhere to help, but it's much more than that. A.R.T. can be upgraded to shoot various weapons!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSo, take a nostalgic trip back to 1987 when games were hard and they didn't make sense.<br />\r\nDeathchron is an NES style game inspired by titles such as Blaster Master.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFeatures:<br />\r\n8 bit style NES artwork<br />\r\nAction Platforming<br />\r\nUpgrades for your mech<br />\r\nVarious areas to explore<br />\r\nBosses that will eat you alive",
